# Miner Llama v5 preset (in progress): Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, UkisAI's Swift-1.5 GSQ-RCO Q2_0 (its n-gram table cut into a
# third shard) on nine P106-090 cards, 65,536-token context, the MTP draft.
# Build: the v5 engine, pascal-p106-v5 at af00bb13b or later (upstream b12483 merged; the taper's cuts=1 landed with
# merge 7ad7608b7), where it was measured. v4.0's engine reads every switch below but cuts=1 (text reuse ran on it in
# R17, on Flint).
# This is v4.0's preset (release/flash-next-v4/settings.env, explained in release/flash-next-v4/README.md) with five
# changes. The first is one switch added, LLAMA_SERVER_TEXT_REUSE=1. On the coding-agent check, two runs with it against two without on the same
# rig, engine and boot (docs/data/2026-11-19_r208_r210_flash_switches/): no turn read one of the model's earlier
# replies again, where the two runs without it did on 4 and 2 turns (1,806 and 3,533 tokens, 23.6 and 19.3 s of prompt
# reading); a task 2.43 and 2.37 minutes at equal work against 2.42 and 2.37, every time measure inside the two plain
# runs' spread; 11/12 and 12/12 tasks with it, 11/12 and 12/12 without. A gain on the work it removes, neutral on time,
# the class that put it into Flint's line (R17); it was added on the owner's word on 2026-11-19.
# The second: GGML_CUDA_FATTN_SPARSE_PASCAL_MIN_RATIO 0.75 instead of 1.0, so a four-token verify pass moves to the sparse
# attention kernel from 6,153 cached cells instead of 8,204. On the deep lane a step is 1.71 and 3.50 ms shorter at 6,144
# and 7,168 tokens, the same below (docs/data/2026-11-20_r69_sparse_switch/). On the coding-agent check, two runs with
# it against two without on one rig, engine and boot (docs/data/2026-11-20_r220_flash_ratio075/): 12/12 and 12/12, a
# task 2.26 and 2.27 minutes at equal work, 30.60 and 30.39 tok/s, against 12/12 and 11/12, 2.28 and 2.32, 30.28 and
# 29.46; inside the plain runs' spread, slower on no figure. Added on the owner's word on 2026-11-20.
# The third: --ubatch-taper short=1400:64 instead of short=600:64, so a prompt call of up to 1,400 tokens (not 600) is
# read in micro-batches of 64. Replaying the recorded agent prompts it reads them 12.56 s (5.70 %) faster a pass, no
# prompt size slower, the same replies (docs/data/2026-11-20_r225_flash_taper1400/). On the coding-agent check, two runs
# with it against two without on one rig, engine and boot (docs/data/2026-11-20_r227_flash_taper1400_agent/): turns of
# 601 to 1,400 new tokens 5.929 and 5.894 ms a prompt token against 7.166 and 6.978; a task 2.25 and 2.24 minutes at
# equal work against 2.26 and 2.24; 12/12 in all four. Added on the owner's word on 2026-11-20.
# The fourth: GGML_CUDA_FATTN_SPARSE_PASCAL_NSM 10 instead of 5 and _MIN_RATIO 0.5 instead of 0.75, so a four-token
# verify pass splits the sparse attention into 5 pieces instead of 3 (two full waves on the P106's 5 SMs) and moves to
# the sparse kernel from 4,102 cached cells instead of 6,153. On the deep lane a step is 99.39 and 99.47 ms at 8,192
# tokens against 103.99 and 103.89, 98.80 and 98.90 at 6,144 against 102.83 and 102.91, 98.23 and 98.32 at 4,096
# against 99.75 and 99.60, the same at depth 0. On the coding-agent check, two runs with them against two without on
# one rig, engine and boot: a decode step 104.05 and 104.26 ms against 109.42 and 107.10; 12/12 and 12/12 against
# 11/12 and 12/12; a task 2.23 and 2.21 minutes at equal work against 2.29 and 2.23, and 2.31 and 2.30 against 2.34
# and 2.33 without the task one control ran to its cap (docs/data/2026-11-26_c1175_nsm10_rig2/). A one-token call
# takes 20 splits instead of 10, about 43 us slower, rare with the draft on (C839). Added on the owner's word on
# 2026-11-26.
# The fifth: --ubatch-taper short=1400:64,cuts=1 instead of short=1400:64, so each stretch of a prompt call between its
# in-call checkpoint cuts is planned on its own and no piece of 4 to 6 tokens is left beside a cut; 14 of the 73
# recorded agent prompts read in one micro-batch fewer. Replaying them on nine P106 cards, a pass took 199.71, 199.85
# and 200.06 s against 205.21, 201.37, 201.78 and 201.75, slower in no size bucket, the same replies on 62 of 62 turns
# (docs/data/2026-11-24_c930_taper_cuts_rig/). Against short=1400:64 the next-token numbers move by a mean KLD of
# 0.004828 (limit 0.028), the same top token at 98.061 % of the positions it can change
# (docs/data/2026-11-25_c981_cuts1_flash_kld/). Added on the owner's word on 2026-11-26.
# What each line does to the replies: the tag at the start of its comment (docs/reply_effects.md; python3 -I
# scripts/preset_effects.py counts them). Here 1 [lossy] (the hop cast in Q8_0), 1 [input] (text reuse), 1 [sampling],
# 11 [order], 5 [draft], 32 [same].
# Use: . settings.env && env $PRESET_ENV llama-server -m "$MODELS/$PRESET_MODEL" -md "$MODELS/$PRESET_DRAFT" $PRESET_ARGS --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
# MODELS is the folder with shards 1-2, the link to shard 3 (the n-gram table) and the MTP draft.
# Every switch is described in docs/switches.md. "Rows" are registry rows in quants/experiments.md (Q...) and the rig
# checks that proved each switch on nine P106 cards (R..., in the data folders named in each row).
PRESET_MODEL=Swift-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO-Q2_0-00001-of-00003.gguf
PRESET_DRAFT=mtp-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-draft.gguf

PRESET_ENV=
# v3.0's preset, unchanged (proved by v3.0's release check, docs/data/2026-11-05_release_flashnext/):
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_PASCAL_KCOL_SMEM=32768"  # [order] which kernel takes a 2-5-token product changes; the k-column kernels of 2-5-token passes take activations up to 32 KB of shared memory (Q823)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_PASCAL_KCOL_TABLE=0"  # [order] which kernel takes a 2-5-token product changes; and run every shape, without the lookup table (Q824)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_HOP_CAST=q8_0"  # [lossy] the residual rounded to 8 bits at each of the eight card boundaries, no measurable KLD (C200k), every type below 8 bits failed its KLD gate (Q963); the residual crosses each card boundary in Q8_0 (Q231, Q963)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_HOP_STAGED=1"  # [same] each hop between cards goes through a pinned host ring (Q751)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_DRAFT_SHORTLIST=32768,8192,2"  # [draft] the MTP draft's output head reads a shortlist of the vocabulary (Q592, Q635)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_KEEPALIVE=decode"  # [same] a one-thread block per card holds the boost clock while a split decodes (Q1021, Q1045)
# R70's candidate and the switches proved on 2026-11-11 (docs/data/2026-11-10_v4_candidate/, docs/data/2026-11-11_r90_v4_vs_v3/):
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_FATTN_SPARSE_PASCAL=1"  # [order] the same kept cells, another kernel; sparse decode attention over the cells a QSA layer keeps (Q230, Q441; R70)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_FATTN_SPARSE_PASCAL_MIN_RATIO=0.5"  # [order] moves verify calls to the sparse kernel sooner, other replies at near-ties (Q1252); a four-token verify takes the sparse kernel from 4,102 cells (v5 until 2026-11-26: 0.75, from 6,153; v4.0: 1.0, from 8,204; R69, R220, C1175)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_FATTN_SPARSE_PASCAL_NSM=10"  # [order] the split count, so the order the pieces are added; a four-token verify in 5 splits, two full waves on the P106's 5 SMs, a one-token call in 20 (v5 until 2026-11-26: 5, which gave 3 and 10; R70, C839, C1175)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_PASCAL_DMT=1"  # [same] IQ4_XS and Q4_K at 2-4 tokens: each weight read once for every token, exact (C722, Q1277; R79)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_PASCAL_Q5K_MT=1"  # [same] Q5_K at 2-4 tokens (the output head in a verify), read once, exact (C690, Q1222; R75)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SAMPLING_TOP_K_ROWS=1"  # [same] one top-k over all output rows in the card's sampling chain, the same tokens (C691, Q1223; R83)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_QSA_INDEXER_ROWS=1"  # [same] the QSA indexer reads each pool's key in its cache cell, not from a gather (C704, Q1244)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_QSA_KPOOL_DEV=1"  # [same] the QSA k-pool tables kept on each card, only changed rows sent (C100, Q640, Q1273)
# R72's v4c2: the rig rows of 2026-11-12 (docs/data/2026-11-12_r72_agent_v4c2/):
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_QSA_KPOOL_STAGE=1"  # [same] the QSA k-pool's small inputs go up inside the tables' upload (C720, Q1275)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_QSA_POOL_MASK_DEV=1"  # [same] the QSA pool mask built on each card (C719, Q1274)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_DRAFT_PREFETCH=1"  # [same] the n-gram table rows a verify pass will read are asked for as soon as each token is drafted (C615, Q1100; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_VERIFY_PREPARE=2"  # [same] the verify pass prepared while the last drafting pass runs, unchanged inputs not copied again (C738, Q1307; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_MTP_GRAPH_KEEP=1"  # [same] the MTP draft keeps one graph per batch shape (C619, Q1104; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_KV_SEQ_RM_BOUND=1"  # [same] removing a sequence's positions visits only the cells it can change, the same cells and head (C740, Q1309; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SERVER_YIELD=2"  # [same] a speculative step yields to the server's reader thread once, and wakes it only when a read waits (C741, Q1310; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_MTP_EMBD_FIRST=1"  # [same] the draft's graph starts with its token rows' gather (C771, Q1357; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_MTP_DRAFT_CAP=1"  # [same] no drafting pass whose token the server would cut at a reply's end (C744, Q1314; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_MTP_SKIP_LAST_ROW=1"  # [same] the last drafting pass copies no hidden row to the host (C742, Q1311; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_GRAPHS_FORCE=1"  # [same] prompt micro-batches and the draft's catch-up captured as CUDA graphs without the two-call warm-up (C702, Q1240; R123a)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_MTP_KV_ONLY=1"  # [same] a draft pass with no output row writes only the draft layer's caches (C620, Q1105; R123a)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_MTP_CATCHUP_OVERLAP=1"  # [same] the draft catches up on a prompt call while the next call starts through the cards (C703, Q1242; R123a)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_PASCAL_Q3K_MT=1"  # [same] Q3_K at 2-8 tokens read once, exact (C726, Q1285; R120b)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_PASCAL_GLU_MT=1"  # [same] the shared expert's gate, up and SWIGLU at 2-8 tokens as one launch, exact (C757, Q1333; R120b)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_PASCAL_Q6K_MT=1"  # [same] Q6_K at 2-4 tokens read once, exact (C727, Q1286; R120b)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SPEC_REJECT_STOP=1"  # [draft] only draws behind an accepted end of turn, never output; probabilistic verification stops at an accepted end of turn (C675, Q1187; FN66)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_DRAFT_EMBD_DEV=layer"  # [same] the draft's token table on its layer's card, in place of v3.0's -otd token_embd=CUDA4 (C762, Q1340; R123b)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_FATTN_SPARSE_PASCAL_PROMPT=1"  # [order] prompt micro-batches on the sparse kernel; prompt micro-batches of up to 128 tokens on the sparse attention too (C705, Q1246; R123b)
# R142's v4c3 and the rows of 2026-11-13 (docs/data/2026-11-13_r142_agent_v4c3/, docs/data/2026-11-13_r156_agent_v4r/):
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SCHED_PER_SIZE_RESERVE=2"  # [same] the draft's schedulers planned once over the whole memory, again after a change of cards (C803, Q1407; R130; C818, Q1427; R143)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_MMVF_F32_MT=1"  # [same] the F32 shared-expert gate at 4-8 tokens on mul_mat_vec_f, not cuBLAS, exact (C807, Q1413; R132)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_KEEPALIVE_EAGER=1"  # [same] the keep-alive block ends before a kernel's first launch on a card, so the launch does not wait ~1 s for it (C811, C817, Q1417, Q1426; R140)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_MTP_HROW_LAZY=1"  # [same] the hidden-row buffer's second half made only when a prompt is cut into several calls (C813, Q1422; R139)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_PASCAL_KCOL_EXACT=1"  # [order] keeps these products on the k-column kernel, so a verify pass gives each token the sums a one-token pass gives it; the k-column kernel keeps every Q3_K, IQ4_NL, Q2_0 and Q8_0 product of 2-8 tokens, so each token gets its one-token sums (C805, Q1411; R126)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_PASCAL_KCOL_SKIP=q4_0,q5_0"  # [same] the shared expert's Q4_0/Q5_0 downs at 2-4 tokens on the multi-column kernel, exact (C755, Q1456; R150; C828, Q1470; R155)
# v5 (2026-11-19, docs/data/2026-11-19_r208_r210_flash_switches/):
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SERVER_TEXT_REUSE=1"  # [input] the model reads its own reply tokens instead of the re-tokenized text; the server keeps its cached tokens where a reply sent back spells the same text in other tokens, so it never reads that reply again (C884, Q1598, Q1604; R210)
PRESET_ENV=${PRESET_ENV# }

PRESET_ARGS=
# v3.0's line (every flag explained in release/flash-next-v3/README.md) with -b 2048 -> 4096, -otd token_embd=CUDA4
# removed and --spec-draft-n-ubatch 128 -> 512:
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS -ngl 99 -fa on -c 65536 -np 1 -bs --ctx-checkpoints 4 --cache-ram 0 --jinja --reasoning-format deepseek"  # [order] the run line: flash attention and sampling on the cards (-bs, the same distribution, other draws) set the order and the draws; nothing else in it touches the numbers
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --temp 1.0 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --min-p 0"  # [sampling] the makers' sampling
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS -b 4096 -ub 512"  # [order] the micro-batch size sets the arithmetic's order; prompt calls of 4,096 tokens in micro-batches of 512 (R123b)
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS -ts 6,6,6,6,5,6,5,6,3 -fit off -lm dio"  # [same] the layer split by memory; direct I/O load (Q547)
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --spec-type draft-mtp --spec-draft-n-max 3"  # [draft] the MTP draft, three tokens a step
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --spec-draft-n-ubatch 512"  # [draft] the draft's micro-batch: 512 reads prompts 3.7 % faster than 128 (R53); upstream #32078 needs the flag
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --no-host"  # [same]
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --spec-draft-sampling probabilistic --spec-draft-p-min 0"  # [draft] token-by-token rejection of the draft, the reply's distribution unchanged (R70)
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --ctx-checkpoints-vram 4"  # [same] a slot's newest four checkpoints on the cards (Q440, Q548; R70)
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --ctx-checkpoints-incall"  # [order] keeps a prompt's call whole, so its micro-batches differ from a cut call's; checkpoints taken inside a prompt's call, not by cutting it: -18.99 % prompt time (C217, Q1306; R85)
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --ubatch-taper short=1400:64,cuts=1"  # [order] micro-batches of 64 against 512: KLD 0.0127, the same top token 96.9 % (FN95, Q1493); cuts=1 against without: KLD 0.004828, the same top token 98.061 % (C981, Q1714); a prompt call of at most 1,400 tokens in micro-batches of 64 (v4.0: 600; Q771, R60; R225, R227), each stretch between its in-call checkpoint cuts planned on its own (cuts=1 since 2026-11-26; C905, C930)
PRESET_ARGS=${PRESET_ARGS# }
